    "updated_at": "2016-11-22T18:53:54Z",
    "body": "Hmm. I appreciate the desire to solve the problem here, but I am not sure a new property is the correct way to do it. Maybe the best fix would be to tackle #263 more head-on? For example, I think if all browsers did *not* fire keypress when using the Return key to select an option, that would solve your issue, right?\r\n\r\nAlternately, [forms already automatically submit when the return key is pressed if there is a submit buton in them](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#implicit-submission:concept-submit-button). Would this suffice for your use case?",
